IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pip-nouns`
IMPORT `pip-dates`
IMPORT `pip-part7-periods`

-- PART 7 -- PAYABILITY WHEN A PERSON IS RESIDING IN CERTAIN ACCOMMODATION OR IS DETAINED IN CUSTODY: regulations 28 to 31.
--
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Sections 85 to 87 of the Act stop payment while C is in a care home, a hospital or
-- custody; these regulations say which enactments count for the care home condition, who is excepted, and for how many
-- days payment goes on. Each rule answers one question about one day: is an amount payable.
-- out of text: Welfare Reform Act 2012 ss 85, 86, 87

§ `Regulation 28: care home residents`

-- reg 28(2): for the purpose of section 85(2) of the Act the specified enactments are (a) Part 3 of the National Assistance
-- Act 1948; (b) sections 59 and 59A of the Social Work (Scotland) Act 1968; (c) the Mental Health Act 1983; (d) the Community
-- Care and Health (Scotland) Act 2002; (e) the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003; (ee) section 57 of the
-- Health and Social Care Act 2001; (eea) Part 1 of the Care Act 2014; (eeb) Part 4 of the Social Services and Well-being
-- (Wales) Act 2014; or (f) any other enactment relating to persons under a disability or to young persons or to education or
-- training except (i) to (vii), seven enactments about grants and financial support for education.
-- The converter shows "; ..." after (e), (ee) and (eea): omitted words, read as struck.
DECLARE `an enactment under which qualifying services may be provided` IS ONE OF
    `Part 3 of the National Assistance Act 1948`
    `sections 59 and 59A of the Social Work (Scotland) Act 1968`
    `the Mental Health Act 1983`
    `the Community Care and Health (Scotland) Act 2002`
    `the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003`
    `section 57 of the Health and Social Care Act 2001`
    `Part 1 of the Care Act 2014`
    `Part 4 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014`
    `any other enactment relating to persons under a disability or to young persons or to education or training`
    `section 485 of the Education Act 1996`
    `section 14 of the Education Act 2002`
    `section 49 or section 73 of the Education (Scotland) Act 1980`
    `section 65 of the Further and Higher Education Act 1992`
    `section 4 or section 11 of the Further and Higher Education (Scotland) Act 2005`
    `section 22 of the Teaching and Higher Education Act 1998`
    `section 39 or section 40 of the Higher Education and Research Act 2017`
    `an enactment of some other kind`

-- src:404 | (2) For the purpose of section 85(2) of the Act the specified enactments are—
-- src:405 | (a) Part 3 of the National Assistance Act 1948 (Local Authority Services);
-- src:406 | (b) sections 59 and 59A of the Social Work (Scotland) Act 1968 (provision of residential and other establishments by local authorities and maximum period for repayment of sums borrowed for such provision and grants in respect of secure accommodation for children respectively);
-- src:407 | (c) the Mental Health Act 1983;
-- src:408 | (d) the Community Care and Health (Scotland) Act 2002;
-- src:409 | (e) the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003; ...
-- src:410 | (ee) section 57 of the Health and Social Care Act 2001, ...
-- src:411 | (eea) Part 1 of the Care Act 2014 (care and support), ...
-- src:412 | (eeb) Part 4 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014 (meeting needs), or
-- src:413 | (f) any other enactment relating to persons under a disability or to young persons or to education or training except—
-- src:414 | (i) section 485 of the Education Act 1996 (grants in aid of educational services or research);
-- src:415 | (ii) section 14 of the Education Act 2002 (power of Secretary of State or National Assembly for Wales to give financial assistance for purposes related to education or children etc.);
-- src:416 | (iii) section 49 of the Education (Scotland) Act 1980 (power of education authorities to assist persons to take advantage of educational facilities) or section 73 of that Act (power of Scottish Ministers to make grants to education authorities and others);
-- src:417 | (iv) section 65 of the Further and Higher Education Act 1992 (administration of funds by HEFCW);
-- src:418 | (v) section 4 of the Further and Higher Education (Scotland) Act 2005 (general duty of Scottish Ministers to provide support for funding of higher education) or section 11 of that Act (administration of funds); and
-- src:419 | (vi) section 22 of the Teaching and Higher Education Act 1998 (new arrangements for giving financial support to students).
-- src:420 | (vii) section 39 of the Higher Education and Research Act 2017 (financial support for registered higher education providers) or section 40 of that Act (financial support for certain institutions);
@ref reg 28(2) (src:404-420)
GIVEN e IS AN `an enactment under which qualifying services may be provided`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 28(2): this enactment is a specified enactment` e MEANS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `Part 3 of the National Assistance Act 1948` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sections 59 and 59A of the Social Work (Scotland) Act 1968` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Mental Health Act 1983` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Community Care and Health (Scotland) Act 2002` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 57 of the Health and Social Care Act 2001` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Part 1 of the Care Act 2014` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Part 4 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other enactment relating to persons under a disability or to young persons or to education or training` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 485 of the Education Act 1996` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `section 14 of the Education Act 2002` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `section 49 or section 73 of the Education (Scotland) Act 1980` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `section 65 of the Further and Higher Education Act 1992` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `section 4 or section 11 of the Further and Higher Education (Scotland) Act 2005` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `section 22 of the Teaching and Higher Education Act 1998` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `section 39 or section 40 of the Higher Education and Research Act 2017` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an enactment of some other kind` THEN FALSE

-- The care home condition of section 85(2): costs of qualifying services borne out of public or local funds. What else the
-- section needs (that C is in a care home and is provided with qualifying services) is the Act's; it enters as one fact.
@ref reg 28(1), reg 28(2) (src:403-404)
GIVEN `qualifying services are provided to C in a care home` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs of those services are borne out of public or local funds under the enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS AN `an enactment under which qualifying services may be provided`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 28(2): C meets the condition in section 85(2) of the Act` MEANS
        `qualifying services are provided to C in a care home`
    AND `the costs of those services are borne out of public or local funds under the enactment`
    AND `reg 28(2): this enactment is a specified enactment` e

-- reg 28(3): paragraph (1) does not apply in the case of C, where C is a person (a) who has not reached the age of 18 and to
-- whom (i) section 17(10)(b) of the Children Act 1989 or section 93(4)(a)(ii) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995 applies
-- because C's health is likely to be significantly impaired, or further impaired, without the provision of services for C; or
-- (ii) section 17(10)(c) of the Children Act 1989 or section 93(4)(a)(iii) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995 applies; (aa)
-- to whom section 37, 38 or 42 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014 applies; or (b) who is accommodated
-- outside the United Kingdom if the costs of any qualifying services are borne wholly or partly by a local authority
-- pursuant to their powers under section 320 of the Education Act 1996 or section 25 of the Education (Additional Support
-- for Learning) (Scotland) Act 2004. Subject to paragraph (4): paragraphs (3)(a) and (aa) only apply during any period in
-- which the local authority looking after C places C in a private dwelling with a family, or with a relative of C, or with
-- some other suitable person.
-- src:421 | (3) Subject to paragraph (4), paragraph (1) does not apply in the case of C, where C is a person—
-- src:422 | (a) who has not reached the age of 18 and to whom –
-- src:423 | (i) section 17(10)(b) of the Children Act 1989 (provision of services for children in need: impaired health and development) or section 93(4)(a)(ii) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995 (interpretation: children in need of care and attention due to impaired health and development) applies because C's health is likely to be significantly impaired, or further impaired, without the provision of services for C; or
-- src:424 | (ii) section 17(10)(c) of the Children Act 1989 (provision of services for children in need: disability) or section 93(4)(a)(iii) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995 (interpretation: children in need of care and attention due to disability) applies; ...
-- src:425 | (aa) to whom section 37, 38 or 42 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014 applies; or
-- src:426 | (b) who is accommodated outside the United Kingdom if the costs of any qualifying services are borne wholly or partly by a local authority pursuant to their powers under section 320 of the Education Act 1996 (provision outside England and Wales for certain children) or section 25 of the Education (Additional Support for Learning) (Scotland) Act 2004 (attendance at establishments outwith the United Kingdom).
-- src:427 | (4) Paragraphs (3)(a) and (aa) only apply during any period in which the local authority looking after C places C in a private dwelling with a family, or with a relative of C, or with some other suitable person.
@ref reg 28(3)(a), reg 28(3)(aa), reg 28(4) (src:422-427)
GIVEN `C has not reached the age of 18` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 17(10)(b) of the Children Act 1989 or section 93(4)(a)(ii) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995 applies to C because C's health is likely to be significantly impaired, or further impaired, without the provision of services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 17(10)(c) of the Children Act 1989 or section 93(4)(a)(iii) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995 applies to C` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 28(3)(a): C is a person under 18 to whom the children in need provisions apply` MEANS
        `C has not reached the age of 18`
    AND (   `section 17(10)(b) of the Children Act 1989 or section 93(4)(a)(ii) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995 applies to C because C's health is likely to be significantly impaired, or further impaired, without the provision of services`
         OR `section 17(10)(c) of the Children Act 1989 or section 93(4)(a)(iii) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995 applies to C`)

@ref reg 28(3)(a), reg 28(3)(aa), reg 28(4) (src:422-427)
GIVEN `paragraph (3)(a) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 37, 38 or 42 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014 applies to C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the local authority looking after C places C in a private dwelling with a family, or with a relative of C, or with some other suitable person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 28(3)(a), (aa) and (4): the local authority placement exception applies` MEANS
        (   `paragraph (3)(a) applies`
         OR `section 37, 38 or 42 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014 applies to C`)
    AND `the local authority looking after C places C in a private dwelling with a family, or with a relative of C, or with some other suitable person`

@ref reg 28(3)(b) (src:426)
GIVEN `C is accommodated outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs of any qualifying services are borne wholly or partly by a local authority pursuant to their powers under section 320 of the Education Act 1996 or section 25 of the Education (Additional Support for Learning) (Scotland) Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 28(3)(b): C is accommodated outside the United Kingdom at a local authority's cost` MEANS
        `C is accommodated outside the United Kingdom`
    AND `the costs of any qualifying services are borne wholly or partly by a local authority pursuant to their powers under section 320 of the Education Act 1996 or section 25 of the Education (Additional Support for Learning) (Scotland) Act 2004`

@ref reg 28(3) (src:421)
GIVEN `the placement exception of paragraphs (3)(a), (aa) and (4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (3)(b) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 28(3): paragraph (1) does not apply to C` MEANS
       `the placement exception of paragraphs (3)(a), (aa) and (4) applies`
    OR `paragraph (3)(b) applies`

§ `Regulation 30: payability exceptions, care homes and hospitals`

-- reg 30(1): subject to the following paragraphs, regulation 28(1) or, as the case may be, regulation 29(1) does not apply to C
-- in respect of the first 28 days of any period during which C is someone to whom that regulation applies. The days are
-- those of the continuous period of regulation 32(4), counted by `reg 32(4): the days of residence in the continuous period`.
-- reg 30(2): where, on the day on which C's entitlement to personal independence payment commences, C meets the condition in
-- section 85(2) or section 86(2), paragraph (1) does not apply to C in respect of any period of consecutive days, beginning
-- with that day, on which C continues to satisfy that condition.
-- src:437 | 30 Payability exceptions: care homes and hospitals
-- src:438 | (1) Subject to the following paragraphs, regulation 28(1) or, as the case may be, regulation 29(1) does not apply to C in respect of the first 28 days of any period during which C is someone to whom that regulation applies.
-- src:439 | (2) Where, on the day on which C's entitlement to personal independence payment commences, C meets the condition in section 85(2) of the Act (care home residents: costs of qualifying services borne out of public or local funds) or section 86(2) of the Act (in-patient treatment: costs of treatment, accommodation and related services borne out of public funds), paragraph (1) does not apply to C in respect of any period of consecutive days, beginning with that day, on which C continues to satisfy that condition.
@ref reg 30(1), reg 30(2) (src:438-439)
GIVEN `the days of residence in the continuous period up to and including the day` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the day falls in the run of consecutive days beginning with the day entitlement commenced, on which C meets the condition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 30(1) and (2): payment goes on because the day is among the first 28 days` MEANS
    IF `the day falls in the run of consecutive days beginning with the day entitlement commenced, on which C meets the condition`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the days of residence in the continuous period up to and including the day`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST n THEN n AT MOST 28

-- reg 30(4): "hospice" means a hospital or other institution whose primary function is to provide palliative care for persons
-- resident there who are suffering from a progressive disease in its final stages, other than (a) a health service hospital in
-- England; (b) a hospital in Wales vested in an NHS trust, a Local Health Board or the Welsh Ministers for the purpose of
-- functions under the National Health Service (Wales) Act 2006; (c) a health service hospital in Scotland; (d) a hospital
-- maintained by the Defence Council; or (e) an institution similar to a hospital mentioned in any of (a) to (d).
-- src:444 | (4) In paragraph (3), “hospice” means a hospital or other institution whose primary function is to provide palliative care for persons resident there who are suffering from a progressive disease in its final stages, other than —
-- src:445 | (a) a health service hospital in England (within the meaning of section 275 of the National Health Service Act 2006);
-- src:446 | (b) a hospital in Wales vested in –
-- src:447 | (i) an NHS trust;
-- src:448 | (ii) a Local Health Board; or
-- src:449 | (iii) the Welsh Ministers,
-- src:450 | for the purpose of functions under the National Health Service (Wales) Act 2006 ;
-- src:451 | (c) a health service hospital in Scotland (within the meaning of section 108(1) of the National Health Service (Scotland) Act 1978);
-- src:452 | (d) a hospital maintained by the Defence Council; or
-- src:453 | (e) an institution similar to a hospital mentioned in any of the preceding sub-paragraphs of this paragraph.
@ref reg 30(4) (src:444-453)
GIVEN `the primary function of the institution is to provide palliative care for persons resident there who are suffering from a progressive disease in its final stages` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the institution is a health service hospital in England` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the institution is a hospital in Wales vested in an NHS trust, a Local Health Board or the Welsh Ministers for the purpose of functions under the National Health Service (Wales) Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the institution is a health service hospital in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the institution is a hospital maintained by the Defence Council` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the institution is similar to a hospital mentioned in any of the preceding sub-paragraphs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 30(4): the institution is a hospice` MEANS
        `the primary function of the institution is to provide palliative care for persons resident there who are suffering from a progressive disease in its final stages`
    AND (NOT `the institution is a health service hospital in England`)
    AND (NOT `the institution is a hospital in Wales vested in an NHS trust, a Local Health Board or the Welsh Ministers for the purpose of functions under the National Health Service (Wales) Act 2006`)
    AND (NOT `the institution is a health service hospital in Scotland`)
    AND (NOT `the institution is a hospital maintained by the Defence Council`)
    AND (NOT `the institution is similar to a hospital mentioned in any of the preceding sub-paragraphs`)

-- reg 30(3): regulation 28 or, as the case may be, regulation 29 does not apply where C is residing in a hospice and is
-- terminally ill, and the Secretary of State has been informed that C is terminally ill (a) on a claim for personal
-- independence payment; (b) on an application for a revision or a supersession of an award; or (c) in writing in connection
-- with an award of, or a claim for, or an application for a revision or a supersession of an award of, personal independence payment.
-- out of text: Welfare Reform Act 2012 s 82 ("terminally ill")
-- src:440 | (3) Regulation 28 or, as the case may be, regulation 29 does not apply where C is residing in a hospice and is terminally ill, and the Secretary of State has been informed that C is terminally ill—
-- src:441 | (a) on a claim for personal independence payment;
-- src:442 | (b) on an application for a revision or a supersession of an award of personal independence payment; or
-- src:443 | (c) in writing in connection with an award of, or a claim for, or an application for a revision or a supersession of an award of, personal independence payment.
@ref reg 30(3) (src:440-443)
GIVEN `C is residing in a hospice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C is terminally ill` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has been informed that C is terminally ill on a claim for personal independence payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has been informed that C is terminally ill on an application for a revision or a supersession of an award` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has been informed that C is terminally ill in writing in connection with an award, claim or application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 30(3): regulation 28 or 29 does not apply because C is terminally ill in a hospice` MEANS
        `C is residing in a hospice`
    AND `C is terminally ill`
    AND `reg 30(3): the Secretary of State has been informed in one of the three ways` `the Secretary of State has been informed that C is terminally ill on a claim for personal independence payment` `the Secretary of State has been informed that C is terminally ill on an application for a revision or a supersession of an award` `the Secretary of State has been informed that C is terminally ill in writing in connection with an award, claim or application`

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 30(3): the Secretary of State has been informed in one of the three ways` a b c MEANS
    a OR b OR c

-- reg 30(5): regulation 28(1) does not apply to a case where, during any period the total cost of the qualifying services are
-- met (a) out of the resources of the person for whom the qualifying services are provided, or partly out of that person's own
-- resources and partly with assistance from another person or a charity; or (b) on that person's behalf by another person or a charity.
-- src:454 | (5) Regulation 28(1) does not apply to a case where, during any period the total cost of the qualifying services are met —
-- src:455 | (a) out of the resources of the person for whom the qualifying services are provided, or partly out of that person's own resources and partly with assistance from another person or a charity ; or
-- src:456 | (b) on that person's behalf by another person or a charity.
@ref reg 30(5) (src:454-456)
GIVEN `the total cost of the qualifying services is met out of C's own resources` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total cost is met partly out of C's own resources and partly with assistance from another person or a charity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total cost is met on C's behalf by another person or a charity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 30(5): regulation 28(1) does not apply because the total cost is met from private means` MEANS
       `the total cost of the qualifying services is met out of C's own resources`
    OR `the total cost is met partly out of C's own resources and partly with assistance from another person or a charity`
    OR `the total cost is met on C's behalf by another person or a charity`

-- reg 30(6): "NHS trust" means a body established under section 18 of the National Health Service (Wales) Act 2006; and "Local
-- Health Board" means a body established under section 11 of that Act. Reg 30(7): in the application of these Regulations to
-- Scotland, "charity" is to be construed as if these Regulations were an enactment to which section 7 of the Charities Act 2011
-- (application in relation to Scotland) applied. Both are definitions of terms used by inputs above; carried as text.
-- src:457 | (6) In this regulation —
-- src:458 | “NHS trust” means a body established under section 18 of the National Health Service (Wales) Act 2006; and
-- src:459 | “Local Health Board” means a body established under section 11 of that Act.
-- src:460 | (7) In the application of these Regulations to Scotland, “charity” is to be construed as if these Regulations were an enactment to which section 7 of the Charities Act 2011 (application in relation to Scotland) applied.
@ref reg 30(6), reg 30(7) (src:457-460)
`reg 30(6) and (7): definitions` MEANS
    "(6) \"NHS trust\" means a body established under section 18 of the National Health Service (Wales) Act 2006; \"Local Health Board\" means a body established under section 11 of that Act. (7) In the application of these Regulations to Scotland, \"charity\" is to be construed as if these Regulations were an enactment to which section 7 of the Charities Act 2011 applied."

§ `Regulation 28: whether an amount attributable to the daily living component is payable`

-- reg 28(1): subject to paragraph (3) and regulation 30, no amount of personal independence payment which is attributable to the
-- daily living component is payable in respect of C for any period during which C meets the condition in section 85(2) of the Act.
-- The regulation 30 exceptions that reach regulation 28(1) are (1) and (2) (first 28 days), (3) (hospice) and (5) (private means).
-- src:402 | 28 Care home residents
-- src:403 | (1) Subject to paragraph (3) and regulation 30, no amount of personal independence payment which is attributable to the daily living component is payable in respect of C for any period during which C meets the condition in section 85(2) of the Act (care home residents: costs of qualifying services borne out of public or local funds).
@ref reg 28(1) (src:403)
GIVEN `C meets the condition in section 85(2) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (3) of regulation 28 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `payment goes on because the day is among the first 28 days` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 30(3) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 30(5) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 28(1): an amount attributable to the daily living component is payable for the day` MEANS
    NOT (    `C meets the condition in section 85(2) of the Act`
         AND (NOT `paragraph (3) of regulation 28 applies`)
         AND (NOT `payment goes on because the day is among the first 28 days`)
         AND (NOT `regulation 30(3) applies`)
         AND (NOT `regulation 30(5) applies`))

§ `Regulation 29: hospital in-patients aged 18 or over`

-- reg 29(2): for the purposes of section 86(3) of the Act, the costs of treatment, accommodation or any related services are
-- borne out of public funds if C is undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient in (a) a hospital or similar
-- institution under (i) the National Health Service Act 2006; (ii) the National Health Service (Wales) Act 2006; or (iii) the
-- National Health Service (Scotland) Act 1978; or (b) a hospital or similar institution maintained or administered by the Defence Council.
DECLARE `an institution in which C is an in-patient` IS ONE OF
    `a hospital or similar institution under the National Health Service Act 2006`
    `a hospital or similar institution under the National Health Service (Wales) Act 2006`
    `a hospital or similar institution under the National Health Service (Scotland) Act 1978`
    `a hospital or similar institution maintained or administered by the Defence Council`
    `some other institution`

-- src:430 | (2) For the purposes of section 86(3) of the Act, the costs of treatment, accommodation or any related services are borne out of public funds if C is undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient in —
-- src:431 | (a) a hospital or similar institution under –
-- src:432 | (i) the National Health Service Act 2006 ;
-- src:433 | (ii) the National Health Service (Wales) Act 2006 ; or
-- src:434 | (iii) the National Health Service (Scotland) Act 1978 ; or
-- src:435 | (b) a hospital or similar institution maintained or administered by the Defence Council.
@ref reg 29(2) (src:430-435)
GIVEN `C is undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient` IS A BOOLEAN
      i IS AN `an institution in which C is an in-patient`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 29(2): the costs of treatment, accommodation or related services are borne out of public funds` MEANS
        `C is undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient`
    AND (NOT (i EQUALS `some other institution`))

-- reg 29(3): this regulation does not apply if C was under the age of 18 on the day on which C entered the hospital or similar
-- institution to begin C's current period as an in-patient. Under 18 on a day: the 18th birthday has not come by that day.
-- src:436 | (3) This regulation does not apply if C was under the age of 18 on the day on which C entered the hospital or similar institution referred to in section 86(2) of the Act to begin C’s current period as an in-patient.
@ref reg 29(3) (src:436)
GIVEN `C's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day on which C entered the hospital or similar institution to begin C's current period as an in-patient` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 29(3): regulation 29 does not apply because C was under 18 on the day of entry` MEANS
    (`add years` `C's date of birth` 18) GREATER THAN `the day on which C entered the hospital or similar institution to begin C's current period as an in-patient`

-- reg 29(1): subject to paragraph (3) and regulation 30, no amount of personal independence payment which is attributable to
-- either component is payable in respect of C for any period during which C meets the condition in section 86(2) of the Act.
-- The regulation 30 exceptions that reach regulation 29(1) are (1) and (2) (first 28 days) and (3) (hospice).
-- src:428 | 29 Hospital in-patients aged 18 or over
-- src:429 | (1) Subject to paragraph (3) and regulation 30, no amount of personal independence payment which is attributable to either component is payable in respect of C for any period during which C meets the condition in section 86(2) of the Act (in-patient treatment: costs of treatment, accommodation and related services borne out of public funds).
@ref reg 29(1) (src:429)
GIVEN `C meets the condition in section 86(2) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 29(3) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `payment goes on because the day is among the first 28 days` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 30(3) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 29(1): an amount attributable to either component is payable for the day` MEANS
    NOT (    `C meets the condition in section 86(2) of the Act`
         AND (NOT `regulation 29(3) applies`)
         AND (NOT `payment goes on because the day is among the first 28 days`)
         AND (NOT `regulation 30(3) applies`))

§ `Regulation 31: prisoners and detainees`

-- reg 31(1): subject to paragraph (2), section 87 of the Act does not apply in respect of the first 28 days of any period during
-- which C is a person to whom that section would otherwise apply. Reg 31(2): where, on the day on which C's entitlement
-- commences, C is a person to whom that section applies, paragraph (1) does not apply to C in respect of any period of
-- consecutive days, beginning with that day, on which C continues to be a person to whom that section applies.
-- src:461 | 31 Prisoners and detainees
-- src:462 | (1) Subject to paragraph (2), section 87 of the Act (prisoners and detainees) does not apply in respect of the first 28 days of any period during which C is a person to whom that section would otherwise apply.
-- src:463 | (2) Where, on the day on which C's entitlement to personal independence payment commences, C is a person to whom that section applies, paragraph (1) does not apply to C in respect of any period of consecutive days, beginning with that day, on which C continues to be a person to whom that section applies.
@ref reg 31(1), reg 31(2) (src:462-463)
GIVEN `the days of residence in the continuous period up to and including the day` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the day falls in the run of consecutive days beginning with the day entitlement commenced, on which section 87 applies to C` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 31(1) and (2): section 87 does not apply because the day is among the first 28 days` MEANS
    IF `the day falls in the run of consecutive days beginning with the day entitlement commenced, on which section 87 applies to C`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the days of residence in the continuous period up to and including the day`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST n THEN n AT MOST 28

-- reg 31(5): for the purposes of this regulation (a) "hospital or similar institution" means any place (not being a prison, a
-- detention centre, a young offenders institution or remand centre and not being at or in any such place) in which persons
-- suffering from mental disorder are or may be received for care or treatment; (b) criminal proceedings against any person are
-- deemed to be concluded upon that person being found insane in those proceedings with the effect that that person cannot be
-- tried or the trial of that person cannot proceed.
-- src:472 | (5) For the purposes of this regulation —
-- src:473 | (a) “hospital or similar institution” means any place (not being a prison, a detention centre, a young offenders institution or remand centre and not being at or in any such place) in which persons suffering from mental disorder are or may be received for care or treatment;
-- src:474 | (b) criminal proceedings against any person are deemed to be concluded upon that person being found insane in those proceedings with the effect that that person cannot be tried or the trial of that person cannot proceed.
@ref reg 31(5)(a) (src:473)
GIVEN `persons suffering from mental disorder are or may be received there for care or treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is a prison, a detention centre, a young offenders institution or a remand centre` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is at or in a prison, a detention centre, a young offenders institution or a remand centre` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 31(5)(a): the place is a hospital or similar institution` MEANS
        `persons suffering from mental disorder are or may be received there for care or treatment`
    AND (NOT `the place is a prison, a detention centre, a young offenders institution or a remand centre`)
    AND (NOT `the place is at or in a prison, a detention centre, a young offenders institution or a remand centre`)

@ref reg 31(5)(b) (src:474)
GIVEN `C has been found insane in those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C cannot be tried or the trial of C cannot proceed as a result` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 31(5)(b): the criminal proceedings are deemed to be concluded` MEANS
        `C has been found insane in those proceedings`
    AND `C cannot be tried or the trial of C cannot proceed as a result`

-- reg 31(4): the conditions referred to in paragraph (3) are (a) C is (i) detained under section 45A of the Mental Health Act 1983
-- or section 47 of that Act; and (ii) being detained on or before the day which the Secretary of State has certified to be C's
-- release date within the meaning of section 50(3) of that Act; or (b) C is being detained under (i) section 59A of the
-- Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995 (hospital direction); or (ii) section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment)
-- (Scotland) Act 2003.
-- src:465 | (4) The conditions referred to in paragraph (3) are —
-- src:466 | (a) C is -
-- src:467 | (i) detained under section 45A of the Mental Health Act 1983 (power of higher courts to direct hospital admission) or section 47 of that Act (removal to hospital of persons serving sentences of imprisonment, etc); and
-- src:468 | (ii) being detained on or before the day which the Secretary of State has certified to be C's release date within the meaning of section 50(3) of that Act ; or
-- src:469 | (b) C is being detained under-
-- src:470 | (i) section 59A of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995 (hospital direction); or
-- src:471 | (ii) section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003 (transfer of prisoners for treatment of mental disorder).
@ref reg 31(4) (src:466-471)
GIVEN `C is detained under section 45A of the Mental Health Act 1983 or section 47 of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day` IS A DATE
      `the day which the Secretary of State has certified to be C's release date, if there is one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `C is being detained under section 59A of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C is being detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 31(4): C satisfies one of the conditions` MEANS
       `reg 31(4)(a): C is detained under section 45A or 47 on or before the certified release date` `C is detained under section 45A of the Mental Health Act 1983 or section 47 of that Act` `the day` `the day which the Secretary of State has certified to be C's release date, if there is one`
    OR `C is being detained under section 59A of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995`
    OR `C is being detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003`

GIVEN `C is detained under section 45A of the Mental Health Act 1983 or section 47 of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day` IS A DATE
      release IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 31(4)(a): C is detained under section 45A or 47 on or before the certified release date` `C is detained under section 45A of the Mental Health Act 1983 or section 47 of that Act` `the day` release MEANS
    IF `C is detained under section 45A of the Mental Health Act 1983 or section 47 of that Act`
    THEN CONSIDER release
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST d THEN `the day` AT MOST d
    ELSE FALSE

-- reg 31(3): section 87 of the Act does not apply to C in respect of any period after the conclusion of criminal proceedings as a
-- result of which C is detained in a hospital or similar institution in Great Britain as a person suffering from mental
-- disorder unless C satisfies either of the conditions set out in paragraph (4).
-- src:464 | (3) Section 87 of the Act does not apply to C in respect of any period after the conclusion of criminal proceedings as a result of which C is detained in a hospital or similar institution in Great Britain as a person suffering from mental disorder unless C satisfies either of the conditions set out in paragraph (4).
@ref reg 31(3) (src:464)
GIVEN `C is detained in a hospital or similar institution in Great Britain as a person suffering from mental disorder as a result of criminal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the criminal proceedings have concluded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C satisfies one of the conditions in paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 31(3): section 87 does not apply because the criminal proceedings concluded` MEANS
        `C is detained in a hospital or similar institution in Great Britain as a person suffering from mental disorder as a result of criminal proceedings`
    AND `the criminal proceedings have concluded`
    AND (NOT `C satisfies one of the conditions in paragraph (4)`)

-- reg 31(6): section 87 of the Act does not apply to C where (a) C is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody outside
-- Great Britain; and (b) in similar circumstances in Great Britain, C would have been excepted from the application of that
-- section by virtue of the operation of any provision of this regulation.
-- src:475 | (6) Section 87 of the Act does not apply to C where —
-- src:476 | (a) C is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody outside Great Britain; and
-- src:477 | (b) in similar circumstances in Great Britain, C would have been excepted from the application of that section by virtue of the operation of any provision of this regulation.
@ref reg 31(6) (src:475-477)
GIVEN `C is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody outside Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in similar circumstances in Great Britain C would have been excepted from section 87 by a provision of regulation 31` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 31(6): section 87 does not apply because the custody is outside Great Britain` MEANS
        `C is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody outside Great Britain`
    AND `in similar circumstances in Great Britain C would have been excepted from section 87 by a provision of regulation 31`

-- reg 31: whether an amount of personal independence payment is payable for the day. Section 87 stops payment while C is a person
-- to whom it applies, unless one of the exceptions of regulation 31 applies.
-- src:461 | 31 Prisoners and detainees
-- src:462 | (1) Subject to paragraph (2), section 87 of the Act (prisoners and detainees) does not apply in respect of the first 28 days of any period during which C is a person to whom that section would otherwise apply.
@ref reg 31 (src:462)
GIVEN `section 87 of the Act applies to C on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `payment goes on because the day is among the first 28 days` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 31(3) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 31(6) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 31: an amount of personal independence payment is payable for the day` MEANS
    NOT (    `section 87 of the Act applies to C on the day`
         AND (NOT `payment goes on because the day is among the first 28 days`)
         AND (NOT `regulation 31(3) applies`)
         AND (NOT `regulation 31(6) applies`))
